Allocation and setup
====================

No special allocation, reservation or quota is needed: one ordinary
general-purpose node for a few hours is enough. No privileged access, no
custom images, no multi-node topology.

  # 1. allocate any Linux node meeting infrastructure/resources
  # 2. install Ollama (https://ollama.com/download/linux)
  curl -fsSL https://ollama.com/install.sh | sh
  ollama serve &

  # 3. get the artifact and install it
  git clone https://github.com/huuhuannt1998/pg-dsl
  cd pg-dsl
  ./install.sh                 # deps + qwen3:14b (9.3 GB), ends with a smoke test
  ./install.sh --no-model      # deps only, for the model-free path

  # 4. run any claim
  ./claims/claim1/run.sh       # each prints PASS/FAIL per asserted field

Claims 3, 4, 5, 6 and 7 are deterministic and need no model, so they run on
a node without the 12 GB of model storage. Claims 1, 2 and 8 need
qwen3:14b.

The model pull is the only slow setup step (9.3 GB). Start it early.
